{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386739-werewolves-and-quintessence","id":1386739,"title":"Werewolves and Quintessence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T11:08:26-07:00","id":1386739,"title":"Werewolves and Quintessence","content":"Hi.<br /> <br /> If I use Prime 1 and Life 1 through a werewolf, would I perceive Quintessence on his/her pattern?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:36:33-07:00","id":1386755,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I follow. Considering everything is made of Quintessence, I'm pretty sure you'd perceive the Quintessence that makes up the werewolf's pattern. You might need Spirit to see the whole picture, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:41:12-07:00","id":1386757,"title":"","content":"So, if I do the same over a human, would I perceive Quintessence too?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:46:17-07:00","id":1386759,"title":"","content":"Yes. Life and Prime will tell you exactly how much Quintessence the living thing contains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:46:54-07:00","id":1386760,"title":"","content":"Are you maybe looking for a way to determine if a person you look at is a werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:56:43-07:00","id":1386767,"title":"","content":"Prime 1 alone will tell you the quintessence in anything, person, object, spirit, whatever. This can be a so-so guess at telling if someone is a supernatural, but not accurately.<br /> <br /> One of the older books, not remembering which one, has a Rote for detection of supernaturals thats pretty good. Basically though, with Prime 2, Life , Spirit 1, Mind 3, Matter 1, you can ID any supernatural as what they are. Though I'm not to sure how a Imbued Hunter fits into the mix.<br /> <br /> Mind 3 is needed for seeing the Avatar of a Mage otherwise it only needs to be at 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:57:50-07:00","id":1386768,"title":"","content":"Life 1 Prime 1 let's you look at auras, so if a mage knows what they are looking for, they can identify if someone is a werewolf by looking for an unusually brighter and more vibrant aura of a person than it should be.<br /> <br /> As per HDYDT<br /> <br /> Of course, it's not 100% since there might be the rare case of another reason for the brightness and vibrance or a werewolf's aura could be weakened and dimmed. But it's usually good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 05-08-2020, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:21:26-07:00","id":1386777,"title":"","content":"Ya, Prime 2, Mind 1, and Spirit 1 can all read auras. Like you said though they can be misleading. Really it comes down to how much your ST hides supernaturals vs. allowing them to be easily detected. Our games are about medium I guess. We make it easy to detect that something is supernatural, but not always easy to tell what type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:04:05-07:00","id":1386788,"title":"","content":"Then my question should be different:<br /> <br /> Is the quantity of Quintessence inside a werewolf pattern any different from the one inside a human pattern?<br /> <br /> When a mage gets Quintessence into his/her pattern (because of a Node or a Prime effect), I suppose the quantity must be higher than the one you would find in a normal human...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","user":"Argonot","date":". 05-08-2020, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:32:47-07:00","id":1386833,"title":"","content":"While a werewolf is likely, on average, to have more quintessence in their pattern than a human, it's going to be overlapping ranges. The total amount of quintessence in a pattern is something very poorly defined in the system as opposed to how much quintessence you can effectively pull out of a pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:26:50-07:00","id":1386851,"title":"","content":"See page 507 (508 in PDF) for the Quintessence chart.<br /> <br /> Normal human is 10 Quintessence, a werewolf is 20+Gnosis, and a mage is 10-30 depending on their Quintessence trait. (Which I'd say would be 10+Quintessence in their Quintessence Wheel). That being said, how much Quintessence you can pull out of a target depends on your rolls and ranks in Prime and how you pull it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}